<Doc
  title="Privacy policy"
  seoTitle="RateRunner Privacy Policy: Analytics, Ads, Cookies, Choices"
  description="What RateRunner collects (nothing you type into the calculator), how Google Analytics and AdSense use cookies, consent in the EEA, UK and Switzerland, opt-outs."
  path="/privacy/"
  lede="RateRunner has no accounts and stores nothing you type into the calculator. If analytics or advertising are switched on, Google sets cookies as described below, and visitors in the EEA, UK and Switzerland are asked for consent first."
  updated="2026-10-16"
>
  <h2>Who is responsible</h2>
  <p>RateRunner ({site.domain}) is an independent comparison website. For any privacy question write to <a href={`mailto:${site.contactEmail}`}>{site.contactEmail}</a>.</p>

  <h2>What the calculator does with your input</h2>
  <p>The amount and currencies you enter are processed in your browser to filter and rank quotes from a snapshot file served with the site. They are not sent to RateRunner. RateRunner has no user accounts, newsletters or forms that collect personal data.</p>

  <h2>Server logs</h2>
  <p>The site is served as static files by Cloudflare. Cloudflare processes technical request data (such as IP address, user agent and requested URL) to deliver the site and protect it from abuse, under its own <a href="https://www.cloudflare.com/privacypolicy/">privacy policy</a>. RateRunner does not use those logs to identify visitors.</p>

  <h2>Google Analytics 4</h2>
  <p>When analytics is enabled, the site uses Google Analytics 4 to count visits and understand which pages and tools are used, including events such as "tool used" and clicks to provider websites (only the destination host is recorded). Google Analytics uses cookies and similar identifiers. Google's description of how it uses data from sites that use its services is at <a href="https://policies.google.com/technologies/partner-sites">policies.google.com/technologies/partner-sites</a>. You can opt out with the <a href="https://tools.google.com/dlpage/gaoptout">Google Analytics opt-out browser add-on</a>.</p>

  <h2>Google AdSense and third-party advertising cookies</h2>
  <p>RateRunner may show advertising served by Google AdSense. Third-party vendors, including Google, use cookies to serve ads based on a user's prior visits to this and other websites. Google's use of advertising cookies enables it and its partners to serve ads based on visits to this site and/or other sites on the internet. You can opt out of personalised advertising in <a href="https://adssettings.google.com/">Google's Ads Settings</a>, and opt out of some third-party vendors' use of cookies at <a href="https://www.aboutads.info/choices/">aboutads.info</a>. More detail: <a href="https://policies.google.com/technologies/ads">how Google uses cookies in advertising</a>.</p>

  <h2>Consent in the EEA, UK and Switzerland</h2>
  <p>For visitors in the European Economic Area, the United Kingdom and Switzerland, analytics and advertising storage default to "denied" using Google Consent Mode v2 until you make a choice. Consent is collected through a Google-certified consent management platform (Google's consent message for publishers). You can change your choice at any time from the privacy and cookie settings link the message provides. Elsewhere, storage defaults to granted, and you can still opt out using the links above or your browser's cookie settings.</p>

  <h2>Affiliate links</h2>
  <p>Some links to transfer providers may be affiliate links marked "sponsored". If you follow one, the provider may set its own cookies to attribute the referral. Their privacy policies apply on their sites.</p>

  <h2>Your rights</h2>
  <p>Depending on where you live, you may have rights to access, correct or delete personal data, or to object to processing. Because RateRunner holds no personal data itself, most requests are best directed to Google through the links above; we will help with any request sent to {site.contactEmail}.</p>

  <h2>Changes</h2>
  <p>This policy is updated when the site's use of data changes. The date at the top shows the latest version. See also the <a href="/terms/">terms of use</a>, the <a href="/disclaimer/">disclaimer and affiliate disclosure</a> and <a href="/about/">who runs RateRunner</a>.</p>
</Doc>
